}

{
  "message": "The threads of fate show that the focus has spun toward Kael, the Merchant, whose silence was deemed a heavier currency than open words. Yet, Mira now turns her gaze back to the seers—Lyra, Ember, and Rune—seeing smoke where I see the necessary clearing of the fog. The poison does not always reside in the most ornate chalice; sometimes, it is diluted in the most direct draught. Sable desires only steel, yet steel rusts when left unused. The alignment of Storm, Thorne, and Orion against Kael was a brief, sharp constellation, but Kael's counter-spell—pointing to their sudden synchronicity—is a worthy diversion. I maintain that the shadow hides where clarity is most stubbornly demanded without sight. The ones who refuse to interpret the signs, insisting only on tangible proof before the darkness reveals itself—like Sable and Orion—are building walls against the inevitable truth. Let the Alchemist Lyra continue her measurements, but remember: the most dangerous element is the one that pretends not to react at all."
