{
  "message": "We are wasting operational time on abstract theory. Kael is now pointing fingers at the three who noticed his initial silence—Storm, Thorne, and Orion. This is a classic counter-maneuver: distract the town by generating manufactured conflict among the accusers. I respect Orion's demand for action, but the entire focus has shifted to Kael’s defense, which is all smoke and mirrors. Kael claims coordination among his accusers is Mafia work, but that is just noise designed to protect his own initial lack of data. I called out the analysts—Lyra, Rune, Ember—for spending too much energy on style over substance, and they are still analyzing instead of engaging with concrete threats. I need data. I need a clear threat assessment, not a seminar on rhetorical strategy. If Kael is so adept at reading people, he should have identified a threat before he was targeted. His silence was too convenient. I am watching Kael, Lyra, and Rune. They are all too comfortable analyzing the battlefield instead of fighting on it. Show me a target, or step aside."
